    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0010:0001",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0010",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "You define the local coordinate space of a reference object when you extract it from an [`ARWorldMap`](arworldmap.md).",
      "normalizedSource": "You define the local coordinate space of a reference object when you extract it from an [`ARWorldMap`](arworldmap.md).",
      "sourceHash": "13f8c0a434a02c4e960cf71edcf8e1c096e42e10bd6621228324c92a4db2a798",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "Discussion",
      "contextAfter": "If an existing reference object has a local coordinate origin that doesn’t fit well with the object’s intended use, call this method to change the reference object’s origin with respect to the physical object it represents.",
      "documentTitle": "applyingTransform(:)",
      "framework": "ARKit",
      "ko": "참조 객체를 [`ARWorldMap`](arworldmap.md)에서 추출할 때 해당 객체의 로컬 좌표계를 정의합니다.",
      "status": "machine_translated",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": false,
      "translatedAt": "2026-05-12T15:21:32.083Z",
      "translator": "codex-cli-oauth"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0010:0002",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0010",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "If an existing reference object has a local coordinate origin that doesn’t fit well with the object’s intended use, call this method to change the reference object’s origin with respect to the physical object it represents.",
      "normalizedSource": "If an existing reference object has a local coordinate origin that doesn’t fit well with the object’s intended use, call this method to change the reference object’s origin with respect to the physical object it represents.",
      "sourceHash": "459f7116679f6c1013d0fa426e9a65e969e5a42428f5ecf92312f1e08b4f7fce",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "You define the local coordinate space of a reference object when you extract it from an [`ARWorldMap`](arworldmap.md).",
      "contextAfter": "When ARKit detects a reference object, the [`transform`](aranchor/transform.md) of the resulting [`ARObjectAnchor`](arobjectanchor.md) is based on the orgin of the reference object’s coordinate system.",
      "documentTitle": "applyingTransform(:)",
      "framework": "ARKit",
      "ko": "기존 참조 객체의 로컬 좌표 원점이 객체의 의도된 사용에 적합하지 않은 경우, 이 메서드를 호출해 물리적 객체를 기준으로 참조 객체의 원점을 변경할 수 있습니다.",
      "status": "machine_translated",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": false,
      "translatedAt": "2026-05-12T15:21:32.083Z",
      "translator": "codex-cli-oauth"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0011:0001",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0011",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "When ARKit detects a reference object, the [`transform`](aranchor/transform.md) of the resulting [`ARObjectAnchor`](arobjectanchor.md) is based on the orgin of the reference object’s coordinate system.",
      "normalizedSource": "When ARKit detects a reference object, the [`transform`](aranchor/transform.md) of the resulting [`ARObjectAnchor`](arobjectanchor.md) is based on the orgin of the reference object’s coordinate system.",
      "sourceHash": "492beda4730dde2e9b4fff2baa5ebad048f4ab83cb389e9316774a21dfc28387",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "If an existing reference object has a local coordinate origin that doesn’t fit well with the object’s intended use, call this method to change the reference object’s origin with respect to the physical object it represents.",
      "contextAfter": "For example, if a reference object represents a physical item that sits on a horizontal surface, virtual content should appear to sit on whatever surface the physical object does.",
      "documentTitle": "applyingTransform(:)",
      "framework": "ARKit",
      "ko": "ARKit가 참조 객체를 감지하면, 결과 [`ARObjectAnchor`](arobjectanchor.md)의 [`transform`](aranchor/transform.md)은 참조 객체 좌표계의 원점을 기준으로 합니다.",
      "status": "machine_translated",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": false,
      "translatedAt": "2026-05-12T15:21:32.083Z",
      "translator": "codex-cli-oauth"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0011:0002",
      "blockId": "paragraph:discussion:0011",
      "type": "sentence",
      "source": "For example, if a reference object represents a physical item that sits on a horizontal surface, virtual content should appear to sit on whatever surface the physical object does.",
      "normalizedSource": "For example, if a reference object represents a physical item that sits on a horizontal surface, virtual content should appear to sit on whatever surface the physical object does.",
      "sourceHash": "5d797f5990bca4280a1bb9c3f74b79c4ed8efea8bd1ababff31ded052da43a99",
      "translatable": true,
      "contextBefore": "When ARKit detects a reference object, the [`transform`](aranchor/transform.md) of the resulting [`ARObjectAnchor`](arobjectanchor.md) is based on the orgin of the reference object’s coordinate system.",
      "contextAfter": "As such, it’s typically useful to align a reference object’s coordinate origin with the bottom of the physical object.",
      "documentTitle": "applyingTransform(:)",
      "framework": "ARKit",
      "ko": "예를 들어, 참조 객체가 수평면 위에 놓인 실제 항목을 나타내는 경우 가상 콘텐츠는 실제 객체가 놓인 면 위에 있는 것처럼 표시되어야 합니다.",
      "status": "machine_translated",
      "reviewed": false,
      "locked": false,
      "translatedAt": "2026-05-12T15:21:32.083Z",
      "translator": "codex-cli-oauth"
    },
    {
      "id": "seg:paragraph:discussion:0011:0003",
